==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*fulką||people}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|folk|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|folk|lang=osx}}, Old Dutch {{term|folk|lang=odt}} (Dutch {{term|volk|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|folk|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Volk|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|folk|lang=non}}, {{term|fólk|lang=non}}. Possibly ultimately from a {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*pl̥h₁-go-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/folk/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n}}

# [[people]], [[nation]], [[race]]
# [[army]]
# {{context|in the plural|lang=ang}} people in general

